21,5608588503,5608695989,5608828028,5608935961,5609221046,5609269429,5609280086,5609364335,5609495079,5609541436,5609695781,5609823325,5609858511,5609923088,5610093202,5610172868,5610401756,5610513991,5610515462,5610554759,5610589942,5610713463,5610917078,5610973195,5611400932,5611523788,5611595016,5611671404,5611833027,5611956600,5612109515,5612187484,5612284156,5612357573,5612866704,5620026160,5620359674,5620451249,5620654372,5620814939,5623027445,5623140277,5623239329,5623283967,5623331172,5623405546,5623464530,5623486701,5623638759,5624190425,5631134927,5631242964,5632215369],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nDeferred nested-pipeline failures can lose server-error confirmation and receive incorrect error classifications on spans and duration metrics.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Preserve deferred nested Redis error identity during detachment</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200bjedis/\u200bjedis-common/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bjedis/\u200bcommon/\u200bJedisRequestContext.java:115`\n\n[Javaagent] A nested pipeline's deferred response loses its server-error confirmation here. In a Jedis 4.0.0 response `Builder`, save the `Response` from `nested.get(\"wrong-type\")` on another client, call `nested.sync()`, then call `response.get()`. The sync captures `WRONGTYPE` but returns normally, so this guard transfers no confirmation. The subsequent `get()` throws that same exception, which the outer `syncAndReturnAll()` returns as a failed result. The outer span and duration metric therefore use the exception class instead of `WRONGTYPE`.\n\nPreserve captured error identities when detaching, including normal nested-batch completion, without setting the enclosing context's `firstServerErrorThrowable`. This keeps handled errors from failing the parent while allowing deferred failures to be classified correctly. Add a regression for this deferred-response path alongside the nested-command tests.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5632215369","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5632215369}],"frozen_at":1792785225,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-23T19:53:45Z","frozen_sha":"42ed545ad49e478e856556edde3f7b4f63d54e73","head_ref":"copilot/trask-jedis-redis-server-errors","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":40014966771},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nClassify Redis server errors for Jedis 2, 3, and 4+ on spans and database duration metrics. A confirmed `WRONGTYPE details` reply produces `error.type=\"WRONGTYPE\"`.\n\nPreserve usable ASCII prefixes verbatim. Dedicated server exceptions, non-ASCII or missing prefixes, and client failures retain exception-class fallback. Successful operations omit `error.type`.\n\nPropagate actual failures through command, pipeline, and transaction completion, including error results returned inside batches.","title":"Classify Jedis Redis server errors"},"mode":"publish","pr":20792,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792785228,"generation":7,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"90118556925a432f9754b1f8c2afb4f0","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"51704cce1d2448589acb428b9baabfd7","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/98fb6cdde0b957dd9fac1921637140b3abe6e57b","workflow_revision":"98fb6cdde0b957dd9fac1921637140b3abe6e57b"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":40015073907,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/40015073907"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["f0e019b8c94aecca5a15c75d9a576ca2e0df3a202ccd45d77809ff90288c6122"],"seen_inline_findings":[],"seen_missed_findings":["3412cb6dd75b66e2381b445a5d6f624bcaa63cd31c604e0107bdd9645342e04b"],"stage":"verify_pending"}